From 0883b1e5ea82c9872b5abed6249c2b0dfa66bd4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:18:23 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] plugin,daemon: KubeVirt secondary-interface (NAD) support

KubeVirt topology nodes attach meshnet links as Multus
NetworkAttachmentDefinitions with kubevirtSecondary=true instead of via the
default chained conflist. That changes the CNI contract per invocation:
one requested interface, launcher pod names that differ from topology
names, and peers that may not exist yet at attach time.

plugin:
- netconf gains kubevirtSecondary and secondaryWaitSeconds.
- Secondary ADD/DEL operate on exactly the requested interface
  (linksForCNIRequest fails closed when it matches no topology link); the
  default chained path is unchanged.
- Secondary ADD waits (poll 2s, default 240s, ADD budget stretched to
  cover it) for the peer pod's topology/alive metadata instead of failing.
- The launcher's eth0 delegate call is recognized (virt-launcher- prefix)
  and passed through untouched: meshnet must never manage the primary CNI
  interface of a launcher pod.
- Secondary results are aligned to the requested interface name
  (alignResultInterfaceName) so Multus accepts them.
- Secondary DEL cleans only the requested link, preserves the pod's alive
  status, and sets the usual skip-reverse flag.

daemon:
- getPod falls back from the queried pod name to the topology CR via the
  kne/topologyNode, vm.kubevirt.io/name and vmi.kubevirt.io/id labels, so
  launcher pods resolve to their topology node; Get now returns the
  resolved CR name so skip bookkeeping is consistent.
- isPodAlive replaces open-coded SrcIp/NetNs checks on the ADD path.

Upstreamable as an optional feature.
